{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abi83/interns/pulls/323","id":4845804750,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUJrRQs8AAAABINUczg","html_url":"https://github.com/abi83/interns/pull/323","diff_url":"https://github.com/abi83/interns/pull/323.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/abi83/interns/pull/323.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abi83/interns/issues/323","number":323,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"refactor: plan job gates pipeline jobs from Python decisions (#311)","user":{"login":"abi83","id":71170790,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTcwNzkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71170790?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83","html_url":"https://github.com/abi83","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #311\n\n## What\n- New `plan` job (first job of each workflow) runs the skip/run decisions as Python: `plan-coder-run` (type gate, stale trigger, fix round), `plan-estimate-run` (type gate), `plan-review` (check gate + red-check routing, foreign-bot author, duplicate head, automatic review cap; `workflow_dispatch` skips the check gate and cap).\n- `coder`, `reviewer`, `estimate` gate at job level on `needs.plan.outputs.*`; every `steps.{guard,gate,mode,checks,check,cap}.outputs.*` step condition is gone (new guard `test_plan_gating`). Plan keeps a coarse event filter so unrelated events spend no runner.\n- Logic that used to be bash/step wrappers moved to `domain/` (`checks`, `review_cap`, `type_gate`, `plan`); the `wait-for-checks`, `route-red-checks`, `check-review-cap`, `gate-issue-type` commands, the `gate-issue-type` action and the `verdict summary-for-head` subcommand are removed (unused).\n- Reviewer job drops its coder token / identity / dedup steps; bot logins come from plan outputs.\n- Integration coverage floor 57% -> 59% (measured 59.98%); new unit + integration tests for every plan decision (stale trigger, fix round, duplicate head, foreign bot, review cap, dispatch override, red checks, epic gate).\n\n## Workflow line counts\n| file | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| code-pipeline.yml | 947 | 822 |\n| issue-pipeline.yml | 481 | 478 |\n| total | 1428 | 1300 |\n\n## Deviations / things to know\n- **No bootstrap composite action.** A composite living in `.interns/` cannot check out `.interns/` (chicken-and-egg), and `uses:` cannot take a dynamic ref. Instead the redundant `Resolve pipeline ref` step is dropped everywhere (`inputs.pipeline_ref` is used directly), leaving the checkout + existing `setup-pipeline-python` pair, with the ordering note reduced to two lines in the coder job.\n- Plan outputs are `skip`, `fix_round`, `run_review` (+ `reviewer_bot`, `coder_bot`). `job` is omitted until #320 (event routing) and `review_count` is omitted because the cap is consumed inside `plan-review`.\n- Behavior differences encoded by the move: (1) the review check gate and `interns.yml` are read from the default-ref checkout in `plan` rather than the PR head checkout; (2) the reviewer `Flag failure` now fires on any failure of a run that was cleared to review (previously also gated on checks/dedup outputs); (3) plan and reviewer are separate jobs, so a duplicate-head race between two near-simultaneous events is no longer serialized by the reviewer concurrency group; (4) rejected-type / stale issues no longer mint app tokens.\n- actionlint (CI args), ruff, pyright, unit, guards, contract, integration all green locally.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-10-13T15:47:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T15:47:41Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abi83/interns/pulls/323/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abi83/interns/pulls/323/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abi83/interns/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abi83/interns/issues/323/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abi83/interns/statuses/0b0b806ceeda0945cfd3ac92b3cabcc7f4f2aada","head":{"label":"abi83:feat/311-bootstrap-plan","ref":"feat/311-bootstrap-plan","sha":"0b0b806ceeda0945cfd3ac92b3cabcc7f4f2aada","user":{"login":"abi83","id":71170790,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTcwNzkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71170790?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83","html_url":"https://github.com/abi83","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abi83/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1352323394,"node_id":"R_kgDOUJrRQg","name":"interns","full_name":"abi83/interns","private":false,"owner":{"login":"abi83","id":71170790